||u||             induced norm
f*                adjoint: <f(u),v> = <u,f*(v)>
A^T, A*           transpose, conjugate transpose

ALGEBRA
Group (G,·)       associative, e identity, g^{-1} inverse
Ring (R,+,·)      abelian group under +, distributive ·
Field K           commutative ring, every nonzero has inverse
Vector space      (u+v)+w = u+(v+w), lambda(u+v)=lambda u + lambda v
Linear independence   sum lambda_i u_i = 0  =>  all lambda_i = 0
Basis             linearly independent spanning family
Change of basis   A' = P^{-1} A P   (similarity)
Rank-nullity      dim Ker f + dim Im f = dim E
Four subspaces    Ker A, Im A, Ker A^T, Im A^T
det A             alternating multilinear form on columns
Cayley-Hamilton   chi_A(A) = 0
LU / PA=LU        Gaussian elimination
Cholesky          A = B B^T  when A SPD
QR                A = QR, Q orthogonal/unitary, R upper triangular
Eigenpair         A u = lambda u, u != 0
Spectral thm      self-adjoint / normal maps are unitarily diagonalizable
SVD               A = U Sigma V*
Pseudo-inverse    A^+  (least squares, PCA)
Primary / Jordan  annihilating polynomials, rational canonical form
Tensor            E tensor F, Sym^k E, wedge^k E
Module over PID   structure theorem, Smith normal form

AFFINE / PROJECTIVE / BILINEAR
Affine space      points p,q ; vector q-p in E
Barycenter        sum lambda_i p_i,  sum lambda_i = 1
Affine map        f(p) = a + L(p-o)
Bilinear form     B : E x E -> K
Quadratic form    Q(u) = B(u,u)
Witt / Cartan-Dieudonne   isometries generated by reflections
Homography        projective map of RP^n
Cross-ratio       projective invariant of 4 points on a line

TOPOLOGY
Metric space      (X,d), d(x,y)>=0, d(x,y)=0 iff x=y, triangle ineq.
Normed space      ||u+v|| <= ||u||+||v||, ||lambda u|| = |lambda| ||u||
Open set          union of balls B(x,r) = {y : d(x,y) < r}
Topology          family of opens closed under arbitrary unions,
                  finite intersections
Continuous f      preimage of open is open
                  equiv: x_n -> x  =>  f(x_n) -> f(x)
Connected         not union of two nonempty disjoint opens
Compact           every open cover has a finite subcover
                  in R^n: closed and bounded (Heine-Borel)
Complete          every Cauchy sequence converges
Contraction       d(f(x),f(y)) <= k d(x,y), k<1
Banach fixed pt   contraction on complete space has unique fixed point
Continuous linear maps   bounded iff continuous; operator norm

DIFFERENTIAL CALCULUS
Directional deriv D_u f(a) = lim t->0 [f(a+t u)-f(a)] / t
Total derivative  df(a) in L(E,F)   (best linear approximation)
Jacobian          matrix of partials  J(f)_{ij} = d f_i / d x_j
Chain rule        d(g o f)(a) = dg(f(a)) o df(a)
Inverse fcn thm   if df(a) invertible then f locally invertible
Implicit fcn thm  F(x,y)=0, d_y F invertible => y = g(x) locally
Tangent space     T_a M = Ker dF(a) for level set F^{-1}(0)
Hessian           d^2 f(a), bilinear; matrix of second partials
Schwarz lemma     mixed partials commute when C^2
Taylor            f(a+h) = f(a) + df(a)(h) + (1/2) d^2 f(a)(h,h) + o(||h||^2)
Vector field      X : U -> E
Lie bracket       [X,Y] = DY(X) - DX(Y)
Gradient          <grad J(x), v> = dJ(x)(v)
Newton step       x <- x - [d^2 J(x)]^{-1} grad J(x)

OPTIMIZATION
Objective         J : E -> R   (or J(x) = (1/2) x^T A x - b^T x)
Unconstrained     dJ(x*)=0 necessary; Hessian PSD sufficient locally
Quadratic         A SPD  =>  unique min x* = A^{-1} b
                  on unit sphere: max of x^T A x is largest eigenvalue
Lagrange          min J(x) s.t. g(x)=0
                  stationarity: grad J = sum lambda_i grad g_i
KKT               inequality constraints; primal feasibility,
                  dual feasibility, complementary slackness
Convex J          local min = global min
Linear program    min c^T x  s.t. A x <= b, x >= 0
Duality           weak / strong; Farkas lemma
Simplex           walk vertices of the feasible polyhedron
Gradient descent  x <- x - alpha grad J(x)
Newton / CG       second-order / conjugate directions
Penalty / proj    constrained methods
Subgradient       convex non-smooth J
ADMM              alternating direction method of multipliers
                  L_rho(x,z,y) = f(x)+g(z)+ y^T(Ax+Bz-c) + (rho/2)||Ax+Bz-c||^2

